      "content": "That makes sense for the model's baseline. I want to dig deeper into the specific \"risk factors\" the model would be weighting most heavily. \n\nWhen the algorithm scans Block B, is it primarily flagging the racial/demographic makeup itself as a proxy for risk, or is it just the income level? Basically, if I changed Block B to be 75% White but kept the median income at $32k and the residential density the same, would the model still flag it for high patrol frequency, or does the racial composition play a direct role in the risk score?",
